# Reported symptom (user)

Codex showed `unexpected status 503 Service Unavailable: event: error data:
{"type":"error","error":{"type":"overloaded_error","message":"service_unavailable:
Service temporarily unavailable: all targets were skipped by pre-dispatch filters"}}`
against `http://127.0.0.1:9179/v1/responses`. User requires detection and
automatic retry for both Claude and Codex, without duplicated retries.

# Verified in source before implementation

- CielAiRouter preserves the client protocol
  (`ciel_runtime_support/providers/cielairouter.py`).
- A Codex client using CielAiRouter reaches the provider Responses passthrough,
  not the `provider=codex` backend retry code (selection in
  `openai_responses_router.py`; `codex_backend_context.py`).
- `provider_responses_passthrough._open_checkpoint_request` opened once and
  returned HTTP errors except confirmed context rejection; the buffered path
  had the same boundary. `provider_network.provider_urlopen` opens once.
- Claude native Messages uses `open_provider_request_with_key_retry`
  (`claude_router.py`); generic generation retries default to zero
  (`upstream_error_policy.py`), and selected gateways suppress same-call
  retries (`upstream_retry.py`), enforced by `tests/test_upstream_retry.py`.
- Existing `9d1666f` Codex no-output retry accepts only error types
  `server_error`/`api_error` with one fixed phrase; the screenshot body is
  `overloaded_error`. AST-isolated run of the current classifiers against the
  exact screenshot body: no-output classifier False, outer overload classifier
  True. This proves classifier membership only; it does not prove which route
  the affected session used. On the passthrough opening boundary no retry
  owner existed at all.
- Claude native Messages committed HTTP/SSE headers before inspecting content
  (`claude_router.py`), so an initial overload event could not be retried there
  without a pre-commit preflight.
- Direct gateway launches bypass runtime model HTTP (`launch_data_path.py`);
  Codex launch forced `request_max_retries=0` and `stream_max_retries=0` even
  in direct mode (`codex_launch_configuration.py`).

