# Corrections to earlier wording

- The 60 s value bounds attempt admission, backoff and bounded pre-output
  inspection; each opener's socket timeout is clipped to the remainder. It is
  not a hard wall over DNS resolution or a synchronous opener's multiple socket
  operations.
- Exhaustion preserves the original status, headers and body exactly. The
  retry note is attached to the exception object for diagnostics and logged; it
  is never appended to the provider body.
- The budget is a `ContextVar` request scope. Provider configuration never
  stores mutable retry state; sequential and threaded requests get independent
  budgets.
- Native direct coverage is not uniform: Codex with `stream_max_retries=0`
  does not retry a 200 SSE error event, while the measured Claude 2.1.306
  `MAX_RETRIES>0` does retry the pre-output SSE 503. Do not generalize either
  result to every error shape or host.
- The earlier Claude 2.1.292 attribution and the current 2.1.306 measurements
  are separate observations; see the version note above.

# Not established

- Whether the affected session used the local router or a direct gateway.
- Port 9179 on this machine refused connection, so no live request or log from
  the reported incident was inspected.
- A 503 does not prove the upstream executed nothing; the runtime bounds only
  its own replay and makes no server-side exactly-once claim.
- No commit, publish, install or deployment was performed or verified. The
  packaging dry run is at the existing version 0.2.51 and includes the new
  modules; it is not a publish or install.
- The current `upstream_retry.py` revision has no fresh 31/31 acceptance
  capture. It is covered by the 14:26 670-test exact-file sweep (including its
  dedicated `test_upstream_retry.py`) and by the 14:21 production-wiring suite,
  but no repeated protocol acceptance run exists for it.

# Direction (implemented in the working tree)

One request-scoped transient-rejection budget (`transient_retry.py`) shared by
Messages/Responses/Chat openings: structured verdict only, pre-output only,
default 3 for CielAiRouter (explicit 0 disables, cap 10), 60 s admission and
backoff deadline with socket-timeout clipping, gateway reselection through the
existing overlay, no nested budgets, no replay after any delivered byte,
original status/headers/body preserved on exhaustion. Routed Claude and Codex
launches disable native retry loops; direct launches use one bounded native
owner. Verification and deployment status are recorded in the release file.
